+| `launcher_online.cpp`, `launcher_online.h` | The Online play page: network choice, this PC's server (host, firewall), the server to play on, friend code, friend requests and friends, LAN play over Tailscale |
 | `launcher_players.cpp`, `launcher_players.h` | The Profiles page: each player's name, which one the next start plays (`MKW_PLAYER`), a new one, and removing one (its folder moved to `profile/players/deleted`); the folders and names are `core/base/players.c`. Test: `MKW_LAUNCHER_SHOT=<frame>:players`, `MKW_LAUNCHER_PLAYER_NEW=<name>`, `MKW_LAUNCHER_PLAYER_PICK=<id>` |
 | `launcher_setup.cpp`, `launcher_setup.h` | The setup of the files page: `tools/prepare/prepare.py` in a child process (SDL_Process) with the package's Python, `--game` for the chosen installation and `--runtime` for the executable, and its progress line by line; each setup has a generation so the launcher refreshes its RomFS path once after successful completion, before imports or merges |
 | `launcher_tools.cpp`, `launcher_tools.h` | The Tools page's jobs: `tools/prepare/saves.py` (a zip of the player's saves in `<game>/backups`) and `tools/prepare/steam.py` (the game as a non-Steam game) in a child process off the UI thread, their one-line result kept. The page itself (saves, desktop and Steam shortcuts, the version with Check now and Undo update, Report a problem, the log folder) is in `launcher.cpp`. Test: `MKW_LAUNCHER_SHOT=<frame>:tools`. Add to Steam (there and on the card offered after the setup) first draws Steam's library images in the start screen's look (`launcher.cpp` `steam_art_draw`: the flag or `splash.png`, the logo, the title) into `<game>/steam-art` for `steam.py --art`. Test: `MKW_LAUNCHER_STEAM_ART=1` |
